class PhysicsBasedDriftSimulator:
  Simulate realistic data drift based on REAL dataset
  statistics. NOT random — physics equations used.

  Drift types:
    Covariate shift: P(X) changes, P(Y|X) unchanged
    Concept drift: P(Y|X) changes, P(X) unchanged
    Sudden drift: abrupt distribution change
    Gradual drift: slow mean/variance shift

  methods:
    simulate_covariate_shift(df: pd.DataFrame,
                              feature: str,
                              shift_magnitude: float) -> pd.DataFrame
      New distribution: N(μ + shift*σ, σ²)
      where μ,σ computed from REAL data

    simulate_concept_drift(df: pd.DataFrame,
                            noise_scale: float = 0.1) -> pd.DataFrame
      Add feature-correlated noise to labels
      Maintains real data distribution shape

    simulate_gradual_drift(df: pd.DataFrame,
                            n_steps: int = 10) -> List[pd.DataFrame]
      Linear interpolation between original and shifted

